### Instruction:

## Using the API

To use this API, follow these steps:

1. **Installation**: Firstly, make sure you have Node.js installed in your system. If not, download and install it from https://nodejs.org/. After installing Node.js, open a terminal or command prompt and type `npm install -g @microsoft/teamsfx` to install the TeamsFx CLI globally on your machine.

2. **Login**: Run `teamsfx login` in your terminal or command prompt to log into Azure using Microsoft 365 account credentials. This will allow you to deploy and manage resources for your Teams app.

3. **Create a new project**: To create a new project, navigate to the directory where you want to store it and run `teamsfx new`. You'll be prompted to select an environment (dev/prod), provide an app name, and choose whether to include Azure Bot or not. Selecting "Yes" will add Azure Bot services as part of your solution.

4. **Provision resources**: After creating the project, navigate into its directory using `cd` command and run `teamsfx provision` to create necessary resources in Azure. This includes creating an Azure AD app registration for your Teams app and deploying it to Azure.

5. **Deploy your solution**: Finally, you can use `teamsfx deploy` to deploy your solution to the selected environment (dev/prod). 

6. **Test your bot**: If you have included an Azure Bot in your project, you can test it using the TeamsFx CLI by running `teamsfx bot create` and then `teamsfx bot send`. This will open a new chat window where you can interact with your bot.

7. **Debugging**: If you encounter any issues during deployment or testing, use `teamsfx logout` to clear the login session and start again. 

Remember that this is just a basic guide on how to use TeamsFx CLI. For more detailed information about each command and its options, refer to the official documentation at https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/javascript/api/overview/azure/teams-toolkit?view=azure-node-latest.

