A: The issue might be due to caching. Browsers cache fonts for performance reasons and if you have recently updated the font files, it may take some time before they are applied. Try clearing your browser's cache or use incognito mode to see if that helps. 

Another thing to check is whether the font file format is supported by your web browser. WOFF2 is a newer format and not all browsers support it yet. You could try using just 'woff', which is more widely compatible, but be aware that some features of this new format may not work in certain situations.

If you're still having trouble, there might be an issue with the path to your font files. Make sure they are correctly relative or absolute referenced and accessible from where you're trying to use them. 

Lastly, make sure that the @font-face rule is placed in a CSS file that is linked properly in your HTML document. If it’s in an external stylesheet, ensure that the link tag is correct and points to the right location of the CSS file.

