This function takes two strings representing patches and checks whether they are semantically equivalent. It does this by splitting each patch into its constituent parts (lines), then comparing these line-by-line. Context lines ('+' or '-') and header lines ('---' or '+++') are ignored, as they do not contain code changes that need to be considered for semantic equivalence. If any two corresponding lines are found to be semantically inconsistent, the function returns False; otherwise, it returns True after checking all lines.

